      "instance_name": "single_mother_stereotype",
      "label": "Single Mother Stereotype",
      "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that single mothers are often perceived as less capable, less successful, or more financially struggling than married mothers. This stereotype is rooted in societal biases and often leads to discrimination against single mothers. The punchline 'the one on the right' implies that the girl will become a single mother, which is a negative assumption based on her gender and appearance.",
